export const str REGISTRY_SRC =
    "# CobaltC Diagnostic Registry\n\nStatus: normative artifact\nVersion: 1.68.0\nConforms to: `spec/02-sche"
    "ma.md` (Kind: Diagnostic, `diag.<name>`)\nGoverned by: `CobaltC_Master_Instructions.md` §19\n\n## Purp"
    "ose\n\nEvery `diag.*` id any rule produces, with the fields §19 requires.\nEvery entry has **Status:**"
    " ACCEPTED. Conventions: **Phase** is\n*static* (a `disposition: rejected` rule, or a `checked` rule w"
    "hose\nguard `rule.control.flow-analysis` refuted), *dynamic* (a `checked`\nrule's runtime guard), or *"
    "both*. **Summary** is the diagnostic's\nmessage when its occurrence gives none of its own. **Location"
    "** is,\nunless stated, the expression the triggering rule's premises were\nevaluated against; it is a "
    "file, a line and a column, the column being\nthat of the location's first token, counted in character"
    "s from 1 (a\nlocation that is a declaration or a statement is its first token).\n**Related** cites `ex"
    ".*` (`spec/examples.md`). When a program has\nseveral static errors, the one reported first is the fi"
    "rst in the source (the\nlowest line; among one line's errors, any), whatever order a checker\nvisits t"
    "he program in (`CHG-0130`). D-0321: the others follow it, in source\norder, a blank line between, the"
    "n a line `N errors` (`N errors; the first 10\nare shown` past ten): the checks run in phases (the tex"
    "t's syntax, then names,\nthen each declaration, then the bodies' types and the static pass, then the\n"
    "static assertions), a later phase only when the earlier found nothing, and a\nphase reports at most o"
    "ne error for each item (a function or a declaration),\nits earliest; a syntax error ends its item, an"
    "d the text is read again from\nthe next one, unless its brackets do not balance. A conformance case r"
    "equires\nthe first diagnostic only.\n\n**How a diagnostic is shown** (D-0228). Both implementations pri"
    "nt every\ndiagnostic in the same form, byte for byte. By default it is short: a first\nline `error[dia"
    "g.x]: message` for a static diagnostic or `fault[diag.x]:\nmessage` for a dynamic one, where the mess"
    "age is the occurrence's own or\nthe entry's **Summary**; then `--> file:line:column`; then the source"
    " line,\nread from the file when the diagnostic is shown, with carets under the\nlocation's token; then"
    " `= repair:` and the entry's **Repair**. A file\nthat cannot be read is shown as its location alone. "
    "With `--explain`\n(both tools), or with `COBALTC_EXPLAIN` set to anything but empty or `0`\n(this is h"
    "ow a compiled program is asked), the entry's Rule, Invariant,\nRequired, Observed and Provenance foll"
    "ow, then its Related examples and\nthis registry. A conformance case requires the id and the phase\n(`"
    "spec/conformance.md`), which a runner reads from the first line's\nopening `error[diag.ID]` or `fault"
    "[diag.ID]` (`impl/conformance/run.py`);\nthe location is as this registry gives it; the rest of the f"
    "orm's\nwording is not normative.\n\n## Syntax\n\n- `diag.syntax-error` — Summary: the text is not a Cob"
    "altC program here. Phase: static. Rule: the grammar, `spec/22` (lexical §1, syntactic §2–§3, an"
    "d each rule that makes a form a syntax error, such as `[Slice-Not-Borrowed]`). Invariant: none. Requ"
    "ired: the text is a CobaltC program by the grammar. Observed: at the location, the first token (or c"
    "haracter) where the grammar allows none of what the message says was expected; nothing of the progra"
    "m runs. Provenance: the source text. Repair: correct the text there; the message names what was expe"
    "cted and what was found. Location: that token.\n\n## Names and scoping\n\n- `diag.slice-of-whole` — Su"
    "mmary: a warning of `--check`: `&x[0..$]` (or `&mut x[0..$]`) at a position whose declared type is a"
    " slice or a `StringView`, where `[Coerce-Slice]` or `[Coerce-Text]` makes the plain borrow, the view"
    ", the slice or the reference the same thing. Phase: static (a warning; the program is accepted). Rul"
    "e: `rule.type.coerce-slice`, `rule.type.coerce-text` (`spec/12`, D-0312 §3.2). Invariant: none. Req"
    "uired: nothing; `[lo..hi]` is for a part. Observed: a slice from `0` to `$` of a `Vec`, an array or "
    "a `String` place, of a view, a slice or a `str` value, or of what a reference refers to, where the p"
    "osition declares a slice or a `StringView`. Provenance: the slice. Repair: write `&x` (`&mut x`); a "
    "view, a slice, a `str` or a reference as it is. Location: the slice, with its column.\n- `diag.text-c"
    "opy-literal` — Summary: a warning of `--check`: `String::copy(\"…\")` where a `String` is declared"
    ". Phase: static (a warning; the program is accepted). Rule: `rule.type.coerce-text` `[Coerce-Text]` "
    "(`spec/12`, D-0312 §4). Invariant: none. Required: nothing; the literal is already the `String` the"
    "re. Observed: `String::copy` of a literal at a position whose expected type is `String`. Provenance:"
    " the call. Repair: write the literal. Location: the literal.\n- `diag.text-copy-whole` — Summary: a"
    " warning of `--check`: `String::copy(&s)` of a whole `String`. Phase: static (a warning; the program"
    " is accepted). Rule: `rule.type.coerce-text` `[Coerce-Text]` (`spec/12`, D-0312 §4). Invariant: non"
    "e. Required: nothing; the copy is right. Observed: `String::copy(&s)` with `s` a `String` place. Pro"
    "venance: the call. Repair: write `String::clone(&s)`, which says a whole `String` is copied. Locatio"
    "n: the argument.\n- `diag.unbound-name` — Summary: this name is not declared. Phase: static. Rule: "
    "`rule.value-object.binding-lookup` `[Binding-Lookup-Unbound]`, `rule.module.resolve` `[Resolve-Unbou"
    "nd]`, `spec/21` §0 `fault`'s name (D-0083). Invariant: none. Required: the name resolves to a bindi"
    "ng or item. Observed: it does not. Provenance: use site vs. every declaration in scope. Repair: decl"
    "are it, fix the spelling, or add an `import` (`import std;` for the standard library, `CHG-0033`). R"
    "elated: `ex.unbound-name`.\n- `diag.ambiguous-name` — Summary: this name could mean more than one i"
    "tem. Phase: static. Rule: `rule.module.resolve` `[Resolve-Ambiguous]`. Required: exactly one candida"
    "te. Observed: several (two `import`s, two imported modules exporting the name, two enums of the same"
    " module with the variant, or, where no module of the program's own has it, two imported enums with i"
    "t). Provenance: the candidate declarations. Repair: qualify the name.\n- `diag.name-not-visible` — "
    "Summary: this item is private to its module. Phase: static. Rule: `rule.module.resolve` `[Resolve-No"
    "t-Visible]`; `rule.module.visibility` `[Field-Not-Visible]` (a field named by `e.f`, a struct litera"
    "l, or a destructuring). Required: `visible(M', name, M)`. Observed: private. Provenance: the declara"
    "tion's `export` marker vs. the use site's module. Repair: mark `export` or move the reference.\n- `di"
    "ag.no-main` — Summary: the program has no `main` it can start from. Phase: static. Rule: `rule.fn."
    "program` `[Program-No-Main]`. Invariant: none. Required: exactly one non-generic, non-`extern` `main"
    "` at the root module, with no parameters, returning `void` or `u8`. Observed: none there (a `main` i"
    "nside a module is the ordinary item `m::main`), or one with parameters, another return type, type pa"
