    "nce and the clause. Repair: read only what is needed from it (its length, a comparison, a search's p"
    "osition), or name it in the clause instead.\n\n## Aliasing\n\n- `diag.aliasing-conflict` — Summary: th"
    "is access conflicts with a live reference. Phase: both. Rule: `[Borrow-Denied]`, `[Read-Conflict]`, "
    "`[Write-Conflict]`, `[Match-Conflict]`, `[Thread-Affine]` (D-0213: an exclusive path of another runn"
    "ing thread), `[Thread-Lend]` (a second lend of a live lent path). Invariant: `inv.alias-validity`, `"
    "inv.concurrency-validity`. Required: `¬clash(a, m)`. Observed: `witness(a, m, Σ)` — a live non-a"
    "ncestor path with overlapping target and incompatible mode. Provenance: the witness's formation even"
    "t (which borrow, in which thread) vs. this access. Repair: end the conflicting reference (let its ho"
    "lder go out of scope) before this access, or use `shared` on both sides. Related: `ex.borrow-conflic"
    "t`, `ex.projection-conflict`.\n- `diag.borrow-exceeds-source` — Summary: this reference would allow"
