    "ed path, including through an exclusive reference it holds: `[Read-Ref-Through-Shared]`, D-0218). In"
    "variant: `inv.alias-validity`. Required: `mode(a) = exclusive`. Observed: `shared`. Provenance: the "
    "path's mode at formation. Repair: as above. Related: `ex.shared-is-read-only`.\n- `diag.destroy-while"
    "-aliased` — Summary: this is destroyed while a reference to it is live. Phase: both. Rule: `[Destr"
    "oy-Not-Solitary]`. Invariant: `inv.alias-validity`, `inv.temporal-validity`. Required: `solitary(a)`"
    ". Observed: another live path (a reference, a guard). Provenance: that path's formation. Repair: let"
    " the reference's holder end first; release the guard. Related: `ex.destroy-while-borrowed`.\n- `diag."
    "move-while-aliased` — Summary: this is moved while a reference to it is live. Phase: both. Rule: `"
    "[Authority-Transfer-Aliased]`, `[Relocate-In-Aliased]`, `[Rawptr-Move-In]`/`-Out]` premises. Invaria"
    "nt: `inv.alias-validity`. Required: no other live path on the moved object. Observed: one exists. Pr"
    "ovenance: its formation. Repair: end the reference before moving. Related: `ex.move-while-borrowed`."
    "\n- `diag.move-out-of-field` — Summary: a part of a live value cannot be moved out on its own. Phas"
    "e: static. Rule: `[Store-Binding-Place-Transfer-Sub]`, `[Destroy-Projection]`, `[Match-Move-Through-"
    "Ref]`, `[Let-Destructure-Destructor]`. Invariant: `inv.resource-authority`. Required: a moved resour"
    "ce is a whole object. Observed: a field/element/payload of a live object, or a payload reached throu"
    "gh a reference. Provenance: the projection. Repair: move the whole container, or take a reference to"
    " the field.\n- `diag.borrow-of-non-place`, `diag.borrow-of-temporary` — Summary: only a place can b"
    "e borrowed. Phase: static. Rule: `[Ref-Form-Not-Place]`, `[Ref-Form-Temporary]`; `[Simd-Lane]` (`spe"
    "c/16` §3b, D-0254). Required: the operand of `&` is a place rooted in a binding, reference, or recl"
    "aim. Observed: a value or a temporary; a bit field; a lane of a `simd`, or a range of them. Repair: "
    "bind it first; read or assign the lane, or borrow the whole vector.\n\n## Resource authority\n\n- `diag."
    "no-destroy-authority` — Summary: this code no longer owns the value it destroys. Phase: both. Rule"
    ": `[Destroy-No-Authority]`. Invariant: `inv.resource-authority`. Required: unconsumed authority in t"
    "his thread. Observed: absent (moved to another thread) or consumed. Provenance: the consuming/transf"
    "erring event. Repair: destroy in the owning thread, once. (A second `drop(x)` through the same bindi"
    "ng reports `diag.stale-binding` first.) Related: `ex.double-destroy`.\n- `diag.transfer-without-autho"
    "rity` — Summary: this code no longer owns the value it hands on. Phase: both. Rule: `[Authority-Tr"
    "ansfer-Unauthorized]`. Invariant: `inv.resource-authority`, `inv.temporal-validity`. Required: a val"
    "id source holding authority. Observed: stale or unauthorized. Provenance: the earlier move/destroy. "
    "Repair: move from the current holder. Related: `ex.use-after-move`.\n- `diag.overwrite-of-live-resour"
    "ce` — Summary: this overwrites a resource that has not been ended. Phase: both. Rule: `[Write-Reso"
    "urce-Overwrite-Rejected]`. Invariant: `inv.resource-authority`. Required: the target holds no live r"
    "esource, or its type is quiet (D-0194: then the write destroys it). Observed: an outstanding obligat"
    "ion at the target. Provenance: the establishing/moving event that put it there. Repair: `overwrite(&"
    "mut place, v)` to put `v` there and destroy the old value (D-0080), `replace(&mut place, v)` to keep"
    " the old value, or `drop` the old value first. Related: `ex.no-silent-resource-overwrite`.\n- `diag.r"
    "ead-of-resource` — Summary: a resource cannot be copied by reading it. Phase: static. Rule: `[Read"
    "-Resource-Rejected]`. Invariant: `inv.resource-authority`. Required: `¬is-resource(type(a))` in val"
    "ue position. Observed: resource. Provenance: the type declaration. Repair: move it, or take a refere"
    "nce. Related: `ex.no-copy-of-resource`.\n- `diag.destructor-on-plain-type` — Summary: only a resour"
    "ce can have a destructor. Phase: static. Rule: `spec/07` §1 (D-0075). Invariant: `inv.resource-auth"
    "ority`. Required: a type with a destructor is a resource in every instantiation. Observed: `T::drop`"
    " declared for a type that is not one. Provenance: the destructor's declaration. Repair: declare the "
    "type `resource struct T` (or `resource enum T`).\n- `diag.bad-destructor-signature`, `diag.direct-des"
    "tructor-call` — Summary: a destructor must be `T::drop(ref<T, exclusive> self)`, called only by `d"
    "rop`. Phase: static. Rule: `spec/07` §1. Required: `T::drop(ref<T, exclusive> self)`, invoked only "
    "by `[Destroy]`. Repair: fix the signature; use `drop(x)`.\n\n## Arithmetic\n\n- `diag.arith-overflow` —"
    " Summary: arithmetic overflow. Phase: both. Rule: `[Arith-Checked-Overflow]`, `[Neg-Overflow]`. Inva"
    "riant: `inv.arith.range-validity`. Required: `r ∈ represented-domain(τ)`. Observed: outside. Prov"
    "enance: the operand values at this expression. Repair: widen, or use `wrapping_`/`saturating_`/`chec"
    "ked_`. Related: `ex.checked-arithmetic`, `ex.negation`.\n- `diag.div-by-zero` — Summary: division b"
    "y zero. Phase: both. Rule: `[Div-By-Zero]`. Required: `v2 ≠ 0`. Repair: test first, or `checked_di"
    "v`. Related: `ex.checked-arithmetic`.\n- `diag.div-overflow` — Summary: division overflow: the mini"
    "mum divided by -1. Phase: both. Rule: `[Div-Overflow]`. Required: `¬(v1 = min(τ) ∧ v2 = -1)`. Re"
    "pair: `checked_div` or widen. Related: `ex.checked-arithmetic`.\n- `diag.shift-amount-out-of-range` —"
    " Summary: shift amount out of range for the type. Phase: both. Rule: `[Shift-Amount-Invalid]`. Requi"
    "red: `0 ≤ n < bitwidth(τ)`. Repair: mask the amount.\n- `diag.narrowing-overflow` — Summary: the"
    " value does not fit the narrower type. Phase: both. Rule: `[Narrow-Overflow]`, `[Float-To-Int-Invali"
    "d]`, `[Bitfield-Overflow]` (`spec/16` §2a, D-0118). Required: `v ∈ represented-domain(τ')`. Repa"
    "ir: `narrow_wrapping`, or widen the target.\n- `diag.literal-out-of-range` — Summary: this literal "
    "does not fit its type. Phase: static. Rule: `[Literal-Out-Of-Range]`. Required: `val(L) ∈ represen"
    "ted-domain(τ)`; for a float literal, that it does not round beyond `τ`'s largest finite magnitude."
    " Provenance: the literal vs. its determined type. Repair: fix the literal or annotation.\n\n## Aggrega"
    "tes\n\n- `diag.recursive-type` — Summary: this type contains itself. Phase: static. Rule: `rule.agg."
    "layout` `[Type-Recursive]` (`spec/16` §1). Invariant: none. Required: no struct or enum contains it"
    "self by value. Observed: a chain of fields, payloads, array elements or `mutex` values leading back "
    "to the type, with no pointer on the way. Provenance: the type's declaration. Repair: put the recursi"
    "ve part behind a `Box<T>` (one owner), an `Rc<T>` (shared) or a `Vec<T>` (many). Location: the decla"
    "ration.\n- `diag.static-assert-failed` — Summary: static assertion failed. Phase: static. Rule: `ru"
    "le.module.static-assert` `[Static-Assert-Failed]` (`spec/17` §1). Invariant: none. Required: the co"
    "ndition of `static_assert` is `true`. Observed: `false`, for the program as written or for one insta"
    "ntiation of a generic function (the message given, if any, is shown, formatted with its arguments' v"
    "alues). Provenance: the assertion and the constants and types it names. Repair: fix what the asserti"
    "on guards, or the assertion. Location: the assertion.\n- `diag.static-assert-not-constant` — Summar"
    "y: a static assertion's condition must be known before the program runs. Phase: static. Rule: `rule."
    "module.static-assert` `[Static-Assert-Not-Constant]` (`spec/17` §1b). Invariant: none. Required: th"
    "e condition of `static_assert` is a `bool` constant expression — literals, constants (module or lo"
    "cal), operators, `sizeof`, `alignof`, the limits and the conversions — so that it can be computed "
    "before the program runs. Observed: the condition (or an argument of its message) names a local varia"
    "ble or parameter, calls a function or reads a container, or the condition is not a `bool`. Provenanc"
    "e: the condition. Repair: for a condition that is only known when the program runs, use `assert` (`s"
    "pec/18` §1a); to check a value before the program runs, name it with `const` (a local `const` works"
    ": `const u8 D = B + 1;`). Location: the assertion.\n- `diag.not-char-boundary` — Summary: this boun"
    "d falls inside a character. Phase: dynamic. Rule: `rule.stdlib.stringview` `[View-Boundary]` (`spec/"
    "21` §2h). Invariant: `inv.string.utf8-validity`. Required: both bounds of a `StringView` fall at th"
    "e start of a character or at the end of the text. Observed: a bound inside a character's UTF-8 encod"
    "ing. Provenance: the view's bounds. Repair: move the bound to a character's start (a byte that is no"
    "t `0b10xxxxxx`), for example by searching with `StringView::find`. Location: the view.\n- `diag.inval"
    "id-datetime` — Summary: this date and time do not exist. Phase: dynamic. Rule: `rule.stdlib.time` "
    "`[Invalid-DateTime]` (`spec/21` §2j, D-0140). Invariant: none. Required: the `DateTime` names a mom"
    "ent of the proleptic Gregorian calendar (a month 1 to 12, a day within its month, an hour below 24, "
    "a minute and a second below 60) at most `i64` seconds from 1970. Observed: a field out of range, or "
    "a year too far from 1970. Provenance: the `DateTime`, written as a struct literal or with its fields"
    " changed. Repair: make it with `DateTime::new`, which returns `None` for such fields, or with `DateT"
    "ime::from_unix`/`from_iso`. Location: the call of `DateTime::to_unix` (or `weekday`).\n- `diag.entrop"
    "y-unavailable` — Summary: the operating system gave no secure random bytes. Phase: dynamic. Rule: "
    "`spec/21` §0 `[Os-Random]` (D-0142). Invariant: none. Required: the operating system gives bytes fr"
    "om its cryptographically secure source. Observed: it has none, or refused (on Linux, no `getrandom` "
    "and no readable `/dev/urandom`, as in a bare container). Provenance: the call. Repair: run where the"
    " system provides secure randomness; never substitute a clock or a fixed seed for keys. Location: the"
    " call of `os_random_bytes`, `os_random_u64` or `Rng::from_os`.\n- `diag.hkdf-length` — Summary: HKD"
    "F cannot produce more than 8160 bytes. Phase: dynamic. Rule: `spec/21` §2m `[Hkdf]` (D-0152). Invar"
    "iant: none. Required: `hkdf_expand`'s `len` is at most 8160, 255 blocks of 32 bytes (RFC 5869's boun"
    "d). Observed: a larger `len`. Provenance: the call. Repair: derive at most 8160 bytes from one pseud"
    "orandom key; derive more keys with different `info`. Location: the call of `hkdf_expand` or `hkdf_sh"
    "a256`.\n- `diag.crypto-length` — Summary: a key, nonce or digest of the wrong length. Phase: dynami"
    "c. Rule: `spec/21` §2m `[Crypto-Length]` (D-0153, D-0154, D-0165, D-0167, D-0168, D-0169, D-0170). "
    "Invariant: none. Required: a ChaCha20 or AEAD key of 32 bytes and a nonce of 12, an AES key of 16, 2"
    "4 or 32 bytes and an AES-GCM nonce of 12 (D-0165), an X25519, P-256 or Ed25519 private key of 32 byt"
    "es and a P-384 private key of 48, a Poly1305 key of 32 bytes, a ChaCha20 message that fits in the 2^"
    "32 blocks after its starting counter, a BLAKE2b digest of 1 to 64 bytes under a key of at most 64, a"
    "n RSA digest of its hash's length and a modulus long enough for the signature encoding, and an RSA k"
    "ey size of 1024 to 8192 bits in a multiple of 64. Observed: another length. Provenance: the call. Re"
    "pair: pass keys and nonces of the algorithm's sizes (a key from `hkdf_expand` with `len` 32, a nonce"
    " of 12 bytes, a digest from `hash` of the `HashKind` named). Location: the call into `std::crypto`.\n"
    "- `diag.kdf-parameters` — Summary: the key-derivation parameters are out of range. Phase: dynamic."
    " Rule: `spec/21` §2m `[Kdf-Parameters]` (D-0170). Invariant: none. Required: `pbkdf2` runs at least"
    " one iteration; `argon2id` (and a PHC string `verify_password` reads, which is false instead) has at"
    " least one pass, 1 to 255 lanes, at least 8 KiB of memory per lane, a salt of at least 8 bytes and a"
    " result of at least 4 bytes (RFC 9106 §3.1). Observed: a parameter outside those bounds. Provenance"
    ": the call. Repair: pass the parameters the standard allows; `hash_password` chooses them itself. Lo"
    "cation: the call of `pbkdf2` or `argon2id`.\n- `diag.not-ascii` — Summary: this byte is not ASCII. "
    "Phase: dynamic. Rule: `rule.stdlib.text` `[Push-Ascii-Not-Ascii]` (`spec/21` §2d). Invariant: `inv."
    "string.utf8-validity`. Required: the byte given to `String::push_ascii` is below 128. Observed: a by"
    "te of 128 or more, which is not UTF-8 on its own. Provenance: the call. Repair: build bytes in a `Ve"
    "c<u8>` and check them with `String::from_utf8`. Location: the call.\n- `diag.index-out-of-bounds` —"
    " Summary: index out of bounds. Phase: both. Rule: `[Index-Out-Of-Bounds]`, `[Slice-Out-Of-Bounds]` ("
    "`spec/16` §3a), `spec/21` §1 `fault`, `[Str-Byte-Out-Of-Bounds]` (`spec/21` §2a), `arg`'s `fault`"
    " (`spec/21` §2c). Invariant: `inv.spatial-validity`. Required: `0 ≤ n < N` / `i < len` / `i < str"
    "_len(s)` / `i < arg_count()`. Observed: violated. Provenance: the index value vs. the fixed `N`, cur"
    "rent `len`, the `str`'s byte count, or the number of arguments. Repair: check first, or use `pop`/`c"
    "hecked` accessors. Related: `ex.bounds-check`, `ex.str-literal`.\n- `diag.non-exhaustive-match` — S"
    "ummary: this `match` does not cover every value. Phase: static. Rule: `[Match-Non-Exhaustive]`. Requ"
    "ired: the arms together match every value (every variant, at every level a pattern descends to, or `"
    "_`). Observed: a pattern no arm matches, given as the message. Provenance: the enum declarations vs."
    " the arms. Repair: add an arm for the pattern named, or a `_` arm. Related: `ex.exhaustive-match`.\n-"
    " `diag.unreachable-arm` — Summary: this arm can never be reached. Phase: static. Rule: `[Match-Unr"
    "eachable]`. Required: each arm matches some value no earlier arm matches (arms are tried in order). "
    "Observed: an arm every value of which an earlier arm takes. Provenance: the arm vs. the earlier arms"
    ". Repair: remove the arm, or move it before the arm that takes its values.\n\n## Failure, concurrency,"
    " trust\n\n- `diag.propagate-outside-fallible-context` — Summary: `?` cannot be used in this function"
    ". Phase: static. Rule: `[Propagate-Err-Mismatch]`, `[Propagate-Option-Mismatch]` (D-0130). Required:"
    " the function returns `Result<_, E>` with matching `E` (for a `Result` operand), or an `Option` (for"
    " an `Option` operand). Provenance: the declared return type vs. the `?` site. Repair: change the ret"
    "urn type, `Result::map_err`, `Option::ok_or(o, e)?` (an `Option` in a `Result`-returning function), "
    "or `match`.\n- `diag.spawn-borrow-closure` — Summary: a spawned thread needs a `move` closure. Phas"
    "e: static. Rule: `rule.conc.spawn`. Required: a `fn` value or `move` closure. Repair: add `move`.\n- "
    "`diag.mutex-reentrant-lock` — Summary: this thread already holds the lock. Phase: dynamic. Rule: `"
    "[Lock-Reentrant]`. Invariant: `inv.concurrency-validity`. Required: the thread does not already hold"
    " the lock. Provenance: the live guard. Repair: release the guard first.\n- `diag.trusted-outside-unsa"
    "fe` — Summary: this needs an `unsafe` block. Phase: static. Rule: `[Unsafe-Rejected]`. Invariant: "
    "`inv.trust-transition`. Required: every trusted construct inside `unsafe { }`. Provenance: the const"
    "ruct vs. the nearest enclosing `unsafe`. Repair: wrap in `unsafe` after verifying the asserted prope"
    "rty. Related: `ex.unsafe-required`.\n- `diag.extern-non-ffi-type` — Summary: this type cannot cross"
    " into C. Phase: static. Rule: `[Extern-Non-Ffi-Type]`. Required: `FfiType` parameters and result: in"
    "tegers, `f32`, `f64`, `bool`, `void` (a result), `rawptr<τ>`, and plain structs of those (`ffi-stru"
    "ct`, D-0252). Observed: the first type that is none of these, named through the field path that reac"
    "hes it. Repair: pass `rawptr`/scalars, or a struct without resources, enums or bitstructs.\n- `diag.n"
    "ull-pointer` — Summary: C's `NULL` where text was expected. Phase: dynamic. Rule: `rule.stdlib.ffi"
    "` `[From-C-Null]` (`spec/21` §3f, D-0252). Invariant: none. Required: the `rawptr<u8>` given to `St"
    "ring::from_c` or `Vec::from_c_bytes` is not `null_rawptr<u8>()`. Observed: address 0. Provenance: th"
    "e C function that returned it. Repair: test with `is_null` first; C functions return `NULL` for \"non"
    "e\". Location: the call.\n- `diag.assert-failed` — Summary: assertion failed. Phase: dynamic. Rule: "
    "`rule.fail.assert` `[Assert-Fail]` (`spec/18` §1a). Invariant: none. Required: the condition of `as"
    "sert` is `true`. Observed: `false` (the message the program gave, if any, formatted, is shown after "
    "the location). D-0322: when the condition compares two values of an integer type, `f32`, `f64` or `b"
    "ool`, outside a generic function, the message also shows both: `assertion failed: 7 == 8`, or the pr"
    "ogram's message followed by `(7 == 8)`; a condition `p && q` is tested term by term. Provenance: the"
    " call. Repair: the program's own condition names what was assumed; find why it did not hold. Locatio"
    "n: the call.\n- `diag.channel-zero-capacity` — Summary: a channel needs a capacity of at least 1. P"
    "hase: dynamic. Rule: `rule.conc.channel` `[Channel-Zero-Capacity]` (`spec/19` §3). Invariant: none."
    " Required: the capacity given to `Channel::new` is at least 1. Observed: 0. Provenance: the call. Re"
    "pair: give the number of values the channel may hold; 1 for a hand-over. Location: the call.\n- `diag"
    ".barrier-zero-parties` — Summary: a barrier needs at least one party. Phase: dynamic. Rule: `rule."
    "stdlib.waiting` `[Barrier-Zero-Parties]` (`spec/21` §3c‴). Invariant: none. Required: the number "
    "of parties given to `Barrier::new` is at least 1. Observed: 0. Provenance: the call. Repair: give th"
    "e number of threads that meet at the barrier. Location: the call.\n- `diag.channel-deadlock` — Summ"
    "ary: the only running thread waits on a channel nothing else can change. Phase: dynamic. Rule: `rule"
    ".conc.channel` `[Channel-Deadlock]` (`spec/19` §3). Invariant: none. Required: while `Channel::send"
    "` or `Channel::recv` waits, another thread exists that could change the channel. Observed: the progr"
    "am's only running thread waits on a full or empty channel that is not closed. Provenance: the call. "
    "Repair: send or receive from another thread, or `close` the channel before receiving the last value."
    " Location: the call.\n- `diag.thread-cancelled` — Summary: this thread was cancelled. Phase: dynami"
    "c. Rule: `rule.conc.cancel` `[Cancel]` (`spec/19` §1, D-0204). Invariant: none. Required: the threa"
    "d was not asked to stop while it waits. Observed: `cancel` was called on its handle; it was waiting "
    "(a join, a lock, a channel, sleeping, a socket) or began to. Provenance: the `cancel` call. Repair: "
    "none is needed when the stop was meant: the thread's failure is contained, and its joiner or handle "
    "sees it; to let a thread finish, do not cancel it. Location: the wait.\n- `diag.mutex-poisoned` — S"
    "ummary: a thread failed while holding this lock. Phase: dynamic. Rule: `rule.conc.lock` `[Lock-Poiso"
    "ned]` (`spec/19` §2, D-0204). Invariant: `inv.concurrency-validity`. Required: the mutex was not he"
    "ld by a thread whose fault was contained. Observed: such a thread held it when it failed, so its int"
    "erior may be half-changed. Provenance: the failed thread's fault. Repair: find that fault (`try_join"
    "` gives it); keep a lock's block short, so that little can fail inside it. Location: the `lock`.\n- `"
    "diag.deadlock` — Summary: these threads would wait for each other forever. Phase: dynamic. Rule: `"
    "rule.conc.guarantee` `[Deadlock]` (`spec/19` §4, D-0204). Invariant: none. Required: the wait can e"
    "nd. Observed: waiting would close a cycle of threads waiting to join or lock each other's, or every "
    "thread waits on another, a mutex, a channel or an atomic (`Atomic::wait`, D-0253), and none on the c"
    "lock or outside the program. Provenance: the waits. Repair: take locks in one order; send before wai"
    "ting to receive; store and notify before waiting on an atomic another thread waits to see change; jo"
    "in a thread only after giving it what it waits for. Location: the wait.\n- `diag.result-discarded` —"
    " Summary: a `Result` is discarded. Phase: static. Rule: `spec/13` §3 `[Stmt-Result-Discarded]` (D-0"
    "099). Invariant: none. Required: a statement's value that is a `Result` is used — propagated with "
    "`?`, matched, bound, passed or returned. Observed: an expression statement (or a block-like statemen"
    "t) whose value is a `Result`, discarded. Provenance: the statement. Repair: handle the error (`?`, `"
    "match`), or discard the value on purpose with `_ = e;`.\n- `diag.stack-exhausted` — Summary: calls "
    "nested too deeply for the stack. Phase: dynamic. Rule: `spec/15` §3 `[Call-Stack-Exhausted]` (D-007"
    "7). Invariant: none (an implementation limit). Required: the implementation can give the call a fram"
    "e. Observed: calls nested deeper than the stack the implementation provides. Provenance: the call. R"
    "epair: recurse less deeply (a loop, an explicit stack in a `Vec`).\n- `diag.unwrap-failed` — Summar"
    "y: nothing to unwrap: `None` or `Err`. Phase: dynamic. Rule: `spec/21` §1 `Option::unwrap`, `Option"
    "::expect`, `Result::unwrap`, `Result::expect` (D-0082). Invariant: none. Required: the `Option` is `"
    "Some`, the `Result` is `Ok`. Observed: `None` or `Err` (`expect`'s message, or which call it was, is"
    " shown after the location). Provenance: the call. Repair: match on the value, or give a default with"
    " `unwrap_or`, where its absence is possible. Location: the call.\n- `diag.alloc-failure` — Summary:"
    " memory could not be allocated. Phase: dynamic. Rule: `spec/21` §1/§3 `fault(alloc_failure)` after"
    " `allocate` returns `Err`. Required: allocation succeeded. Provenance: the `allocate` call. Repair: "
    "none at the language level; callers needing recovery call `allocate` themselves.\n\n## Change Log\n\n- 1"
    ".68.0 — `CHG-0444` (D-0321): several static errors in one report (Purpose). `CHG-0448` (D-0322): w"
    "hat\n  `diag.assert-failed` shows of a failed comparison. No code added.\n- 1.67.0 — `CHG-0439` (D-0"
    "319): `diag.lifetime-elision-ambiguous` covers a result that holds references, from several referenc"
    "e parameters; its repair is said per case. No code added.\n- 1.66.0 — `CHG-0437` (D-0318): `diag.li"
    "fetime-elision-ambiguous`, `diag.result-source-invalid` and `diag.result-source-kept` cover a clause"
    " naming several parameters. No code added.\n- 1.65.0 — `CHG-0435` (D-0317): `diag.precondition-fail"
    "ed` and `diag.requires-misplaced`, of the `requires` block.\n- 1.64.0 — `CHG-0416` (D-0312 §3.2): "
    "`diag.slice-of-whole`, the lint of `--check` for a whole sequence sliced where a slice or a view is "
    "declared.\n- 1.63.0 — `CHG-0413` (D-0312): `diag.text-copy-literal` and `diag.text-copy-whole`, the"
